codex
Program regeneration is byte-identical. The independent 3,331-case differential found no mismatch against the literal prompt contract, but found 131 Unicode mismatches against the trusted canonical implementation: the candidate deliberately enforces ASCII Latin letters/digits while Python’s `isalpha`/`isdigit` are Unicode-wide. I’m treating that as an intent/canonical bridge discrepancy, not as permission to weaken the formal proof. Next is a fresh LLVM/Haskell reconstruction.
apply patch
